# PRD-005: Management Mode (Project-scoped CRUD)

## Status
DESIGN LOCKED

## Goal
Introduce a project-scoped Management Mode for CRUD operations on Rooms, Containers, and Items.
Replace the broken global top nav and remove the existing project home “Project Management” tiles.

Management Mode supports:
- Deep-linked management views (rooms/containers/items)
- Filtering by room and/or container
- Bulk selection + bulk deletion with confirmation

## Non-Goals
- Decision Mode / Execution Mode
- Item reassignment between containers (Shuffle Mode owns that)
- Multi-user collaboration/roles
- Offline support
- AI search

---

## Navigation / UX

### Remove global top nav
- Remove the top navigation bar (Projects/Rooms/Items/Containers) entirely.
- Ensure no broken nav remains on any page.

### Project home
Route:
app/projects/:projectId

Update:
- Keep Inventory Mode + Shuffle Mode cards
- Add Management Mode card/button: “Management Mode”
- Remove the existing “Project Management” buttons/tiles (Rooms/Containers/Items)

### Deep-linked Management routes
All routes are project-scoped:

app/projects/:projectId/manage/rooms
app/projects/:projectId/manage/containers
app/projects/:projectId/manage/items


Optional hub route:


app/projects/:projectId/manage
(Allowed but not required; deep links must exist.)

---

## Management Mode: Core Behaviors

### Shared UI elements (all management pages)
- Project context visible (project name)
- Links or tabs to switch between:
  - Rooms
  - Containers
  - Items
- Bulk selection via checkboxes
- Bulk actions bar appears when selections exist
- Delete actions require confirmation dialog

### Item filtering input
Whenever a view shows an item list:
- Provide a text input for substring filtering by title
- Filtering may be client-side (initially) within the loaded list
- Default behavior: case-insensitive `includes()`

---

## Rooms Management View
Route:
app/projects/:projectId/manage/rooms

UI:
- Rooms list (left or top)
- Selecting a room shows a “Room Detail Panel”

Room Detail Panel requirements:
- Toggle control:
  - Default: “Items”
  - Alternate: “Containers”
- If “Items” selected:
  - show all items in this room (regardless of container)
  - show item substring filter input
- If “Containers” selected:
  - show all containers in this room

Delete Room rules:
- Room deletion is blocked if it contains any containers
- UI must show:
  - “Cannot delete room: contains N containers”
  - Provide guidance: move containers to another room first
- Items without containers may remain in room (allowed), but since containers exist in room, room deletion should still be blocked until containers are zero.

(Implementation may also block if items exist; NOT required unless you decide later.)

---

## Containers Management View
Route:
app/projects/:projectId/manage/containers
UI:
- Containers list with:
  - container code
  - room name
  - (optional) item count
- Selecting a container shows items in that container
- When items are shown:
  - include item substring filter input

Delete Container rules:
- Allowed even if container has items
- On deletion:
  - all items in that container are updated to `containerId = null`
  - item roomId remains unchanged
- Confirmation dialog must state:
  - “Items will remain and become uncontainerized.”

---

## Items Management View
Route:
app/projects/:projectId/manage/items

UI:
- Items list (project-scoped)
- Required fields displayed per item row:
  - title
  - room name
  - container code (or “—” if null)
  - thumbnail (if exists) optional
- Include item substring filter input

Deletion:
- Single delete and bulk delete supported
- Confirmation dialog required
- If deleting items, also delete associated ItemImage rows and storage objects (if this is already your standard behavior; recommended).

---

## Bulk delete UX (all lists)
- Checkbox per row
- Select-all checkbox applies to current list page/view
- “Delete selected” button
- Confirmation modal includes:
  - entity type
  - number selected
  - any cascading effects:
    - container delete → items become uncontainerized
    - room delete blocked if containers exist

---

## Authorization
All operations must validate server-side:
- project belongs to current user (ownerUserId == session.user.id)
- room/container/item belongs to project

---

## Acceptance Criteria
1) Global top nav is removed from UI.
2) Project home no longer shows Rooms/Containers/Items tiles; Management Mode button exists.
3) Deep links exist and work:
   - manage/rooms, manage/containers, manage/items
4) Rooms view:
   - selecting room shows toggle (Items default, Containers alternate)
   - item substring filter appears when items shown
5) Containers view:
   - selecting container shows items in container
   - item substring filter appears when items shown
6) Items view:
   - shows project items + substring filter
7) Delete Room is blocked if room contains containers (must move containers first).
8) Delete Container makes items uncontainerized (containerId=null) and confirms intent.
9) Bulk selection + bulk deletion works with confirmation dialogs.
